card.spec:
On a landed chapter the left column has nothing in it, and the page reads as broken: `IN PROGRESS` collapses to the height of one sentence while `MERGED` runs 900px down beside it. Two panels of wildly different height, one of them almost empty, is not a layout — it looks like a render that failed.

WHAT TO DO. The two columns must read as one object. `align-items: start` on a grid is what lets a short panel shrink; the fix is that the two column SHELLS share a height (stretch), and the empty one fills its own space with something worth looking at rather than a single grey line at the top. Keep it in this design system's restraint — no illustration, no icon set, no invented hue:

  · the block heading and its `0 TREES` count stay exactly as they are, so the two columns still rhyme;
  · the empty body is CENTRED in the panel, not pinned to the top;
  · the sentence says what is true of THIS board — the existing wording ("No card is open on this chapter, so no worktree is pinned to one…") is right and stays — and under it, one line naming the move that would fill it (`taskops_assign` is the orchestrator's; do not invent a button, this dashboard has exactly ONE write and it is the comment box);
  · a hairline or a faint dashed field marking the empty area as intentional, in `--hair`, is welcome; anything louder is not.

BOTH columns get this treatment, not just the left — a chapter with nothing merged yet has the mirror-image problem and it is the far more common state at the START of a chapter, which is exactly when somebody is watching this screen.

Do not touch the row, the sub-blocks, the fold from `board.groups`, or the three note cards. Do not rebuild the committed bundle.
